{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Joseph's brothers.</b> Meaning, they set their minds on brotherhood to redeem him." "<b>Ten.</b> Perhaps they all went because of the danger customary in years of famine, for a man's eye grows evil toward his fellow, and over a morsel of bread they would transgress to rob and to kill, each man his brother. Therefore they all went, so that each man would aid his brother. And they also wanted to take Benjamin with them, but Jacob did not want this, and it is this that the verse says: <b>but Benjamin he did not send</b>, etc. From this you learn that but for this reason he would have sent him too with them:" "<b>Further,</b> it appears that Joseph would sell only a fixed quantity to each person, and he was cunning in this for two reasons — one revealed and one hidden. The revealed one — so that no person would hoard the grain, and in this there is praise for him and praise for the buyers: praise for him, so that he would profit from every rise in prices; and praise for the buyers, because he would not raise the price excessively. And one hidden — so that all the brothers would come to him, as indeed happened, for they all came to buy, each one his fixed portion."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:52.733281150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}